cards.description:
Create reader/read.html (or integrate into index.html as a view). Full-page reading experience: (1) Renders book text page by page — fetch /api/reader/book/:id?page=N, display as clean paragraphs. (2) Navigation: left/right arrow keys OR on-screen prev/next buttons. (3) Progress auto-saved: every page turn, POST /api/reader/progress with {bookId, page}. Auto-resume on reopen. (4) Eye-friendly reading mode: dark background, large serif font (Georgia or system serif), generous line-height (1.8), comfortable column width (max 700px centered), adjustable font size (+/- buttons, persisted in localStorage). (5) Page counter: 'Page 47 of 312'. Design: minimalist, zero chrome when reading — only show page number + nav on hover/idle.

---
## Review notes (FAIL)
- **[Duplicate code]** `projects/reader/reader_server.py` — `_save_progress()` (lines ~603–609) and `_book()` (lines ~653–659) contain **identical** progress-persistence logic (set `last_page`/`last_position`/`updated_at`, save book, reload library, update index, re-save). This 7-line block is copy-pasted verbatim between two methods. The Dot standard explicitly flags: "不应复制粘贴，应提取复用." Extract into a shared `_persist_progress(book, book_id)` helper.

All other checklist items pass: Design System compliance (all colors use `--dot-*` tokens), naming consistency (Python snake_case, JS camelCase, CSS `reader-` BEM prefix), edge cases (null guards, network errors, bounds clamping on page/percentage, font-size validation, empty content handling), and brief completeness (page-by-page rendering, arrow keys + buttons, progress auto-save via POST, dark serif reading column at 700px/1.8 line-height, adjustable font size in localStorage, page counter, zero-chrome idle). The missing `reader/read.html` filename is a non-issue since `reader/index.html` works identically and the brief says "or integrate into index.html as a view."

